@startuml
title Reminder Send and Delivery Confirmation - Sequence Diagram

participant "reminder_service.py" as Service
participant "KosmoSMS DB\n(Appointments)" as OwnDB
participant "easysms.gr API" as API
participant "callback_receiver.py\n(Flask)" as Webhook
participant "KosmoSMS DB\n(Notifications)" as Log
actor "Patient" as Patient

Service -> OwnDB : SELECT appointments\nwhere reminder due\n(24h window)
OwnDB --> Service : list of appointments

loop for each appointment
  Service -> API : api/mobile/check(phone)
  API --> Service : mobile object (msisdn, status)

  alt Patient prefers SMS only
    Service -> API : api/sms/send(key, to, text,\nfrom, callback, ucs=true)
    API --> Service : smsId, status=1
    Service -> Log : INSERT Notification\n(smsId, channel=SMS, status=Sent)
  else Viber with auto-fallback (default)
    Service -> API : api/viber/send(key, to, text,\nfrom, sms_fallback=true,\nsms_text, sms_from, ucs=true)
    API --> Service : id, status=1
    Service -> Log : INSERT Notification\n(id, channel=Viber, status=Sent)
    note right of API
      easysms.gr tries Viber first.
      If Viber fails within validity
      period, it automatically sends
      the fallback SMS.
    end note
  end

  API -> Patient : deliver Viber or SMS message
end

API -> Webhook : GET /api/sms-callback?\nmsgid&status&cost&to&mcc&mnc
Webhook -> Log : UPDATE Notifications\nSET status, delivered_at, cost\nWHERE msgid = ?
Log --> Webhook : ack
Webhook --> API : 200 OK

@enduml